- op: discuss  # 2a62
  at: '2026-07-30T17:20:26Z'  # 2a62
  by: agent  # 2a62
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2a62
  clock: 3  # 2a62
  nonce: 2a62  # 2a62
  message: "DONE — DOCUMENT verdict, and the item was partly stale on inspection.\n\nIts stated expectation was 'one of the two fields should be renamed or otherwise disambiguated', and its evidence line said 'Neither is declared in the schema.' That second claim is STALE: both ARE declared, with distinct descriptions — Limits.not_captured and reproducibility_context.not_captured are each present in docs/schema.json. The spec had also already disambiguated the limits side, with an explicit cross-reference to the other.\n\nWhat genuinely remained was the ASYMMETRY: a reader arriving at the reproducibility_context side got no pointer back. That reciprocal note is added, so either entry point now lands on the distinction — limits.not_captured lists analysis-coverage categories static analysis never captures anywhere (a universal static disclaimer, identical for every repo), reproducibility_context.not_captured lists determinism factors, i.e. the disclaimed L3-L5 levels.\n\nRENAME DECLINED, on precedent: each name is correct within its own block, both are declared with distinct descriptions, and a rename is a breaking change purchasing no disambiguation the parent path does not already provide. Same verdict as edge_key vs stable_id (WI-niboh, cross-ref added, rename declined as breaking) and the sha256: surface shared by stable_id/shape_id (WI-tisar, documented rather than reformatted).\n\nWI-latip is the same defect filed twice and is closed alongside."  # 2a62
